the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base termlabel includes these resources:
    lomo.

the knowledge base termlabel includes:

the text of the source description is at "sources/termLabel.ttl".

% Who bears a duty: the agent of this role of the action (lomo.le).
the bearer role is addresser.


def personal data is identified by "http://example.org/Def_PersonalData".

def personal data is a definition.

def personal data has the term label "personal data".

def personal data has the definiendum "personal data".

def personal data has the definiens "any information relating to an identified or identifiable natural person ('data subject'); an identifiable natural person is one who can be identified, directly or indirectly, in particular by reference to an identifier such as a name, an identification number, location data, an online identifier or to one or more factors specific to the physical, physiological, genetic, mental, economic, cultural or social identity of that natural person".

def personal data is established in "https://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679/art_4/par_1".


% The questions of LOMO's requirements document (its competency questions),
% as far as a description can answer them.
query parts is:
    which thing is part of the description.

query kinds is:
    which thing is of the kind which kind.

query bearer is:
    the bearer role is which role.

query rules_of_act is:
    which rule is established by the act which act.

query provisions is:
    which thing is established in which provision.

query places is:
    which rule is laid down in which place.

query joint_rules is:
    which rule is established in more than one provision.

query prescriptive is:
    which thing is a prescriptive rule.

query constitutive is:
    which thing is a constitutive rule.

query definitions is:
    which thing is a definition.

query definienda is:
    which definition has the definiendum which text.

query definientia is:
    which definition has the definiens which text.

query rules_without_conditions is:
    which rule has no written conditions.

query applies is:
    which rule applies to which party.

query texts is:
    which thing is described by the text which text.

query addresses is:
    which thing is identified by which address.

